  regime 0   Wald chi2(2) =     4.32   Prob > chi2 = 0.1153
  cubic terms (u^3-3u, both regimes) Wald chi2(2) =    13.35   Prob > chi2 = 0.0013
Reading: (a) rejects when the regime laws are not normal (the likelihood is then
inconsistent, the two-step is not); (b) rejects when E[omega_j | u] bends (both routes
lose the curve; the augmented two-step, esreg ..., method(twostep) hermite(#), fits it,
of order 3 if the cubic terms reject, else 2; the semiparametric MTE of esrmte checks it).

